{"id": "3255b4ee-e6cd-4e1b-8bcf-80e5c76bb4a4", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll run this in two parallel passes: one for cluster-level controls and one for node-level controls. Each pass records every denied read, so I can tell you which controls it affected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_HiYg0YDelcekUaMdEWbQVj", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "eks-cis-cluster-level", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "verifying-with-docs", "discovering-topology", "searching-logs"], "prompt": "[DEEP RESEARCH MODE]
{
  "task": "Read-only compliance assessment of EKS cluster 'cis-skill-test' (us-east-1, AWS account 012345678901_1) for the CLUSTER-LEVEL half of the check. Cover: (a) CIS Amazon EKS Benchmark v1.8.0 section 2 (Control Plane Configuration, e.g. 2.1.1 audit logging), section 4 (Policies: RBAC 4.1.x, Pod Security 4.2.x, CNI/network policy 4.3.x, secrets 4.4.x, general policies 4.5.x) and section 5 (Managed Services: 5.1 image scanning/ECR, 5.2 IAM/least privilege, 5.3 KMS envelope encryption of secrets, 5.4 cluster networking: endpoint public/private access, public access CIDRs, private nodes, network policy, 5.5 authentication/authorization incl. IAM authenticator/access entries, 5.6 other e.g. namespaces/default SA). (b) Supplementary checks: AWS-1 audit logging (all control-plane log types enabled?), AWS-2 cluster Kubernetes version support status (compare with EKS supported/extended-support versions; today is 2026-11-19), AWS-4 GuardDuty EKS protection (audit log monitoring + runtime monitoring detectors/features), AWS-5 CloudTrail (trail exists, multi-region, logging on, log validation), AWS-9 backup (AWS Backup plans/selections covering the cluster/its persistent volumes/etcd-relevant resources, or Velero etc. evidence).",
  "context": "User wants EVERY control of the benchmark section assigned here to get a status (PASS / FAIL / MANUAL / NOT ASSESSABLE) with concrete evidence (API call used, key fields/values, resource IDs). Use only read-only AWS calls (eks describe/list, iam get/list, ec2 describe, guardduty, cloudtrail describe/get via the proper CloudTrail route, backup list/get, ecr describe, etc.). Controls that need Kubernetes API access (RBAC, pod security, network policy objects, secrets, namespaces) should be assessed via EKS access entries / AWS APIs where possible; if the Kubernetes API is not reachable with the tools you have, mark those controls NOT ASSESSABLE and say exactly why — do NOT guess or fabricate. Use the AWS docs lookup tool to confirm the exact v1.8.0 control IDs/titles if unsure; list every control individually with its ID and title.",
  "resources": ["EKS cluster cis-skill-test", "us-east-1", "account 012345678901_1"],
  "criteria": "CRITICAL: Keep an explicit log of EVERY read call that was denied or errored (AccessDenied, UnauthorizedOperation, etc.): exact service:Action, resource, and error text, and for each denial list which control IDs could not be fully verified because of it. Return a table: Control ID | Title | Status | Evidence, followed by a 'Denied reads' table: Call | Error | Controls affected. Another agent covers node-level controls (CIS section 3 worker nodes, AWS-3, AWS-6, AWS-7, AWS-8) — do not duplicate them."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check cluster-level EKS CIS controls and AWS-1, 2, 4, 5, 9"}, {"id": "tooluse_Ix8kP4GYeTJZrdKLW0jFPh", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "eks-cis-node-level", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["verifying-with-docs", "discovering-topology", "exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "[DEEP RESEARCH MODE]
{
  "task": "Read-only compliance assessment of the NODE-LEVEL half for EKS cluster 'cis-skill-test' (us-east-1, AWS account 012345678901_1). Cover: (a) CIS Amazon EKS Benchmark v1.8.0 section 3 (Worker Nodes): 3.1.x worker node configuration files (kubeconfig/kubelet service file permissions & ownership, kubelet config file), 3.2.x kubelet settings (anonymous auth disabled, authorization mode not AlwaysAllow, client CA file, read-only port, streaming connection idle timeout, protect-kernel-defaults, iptables util chains, hostname-override, eventRecordQPS, rotate-certificates, RotateKubeletServerCertificate, etc.), 3.3.1 container image registry (prefer ECR). (b) Supplementary checks: AWS-3 managed node group / Fargate / self-managed node Kubernetes version support and skew vs control plane, AMI release versions; AWS-6 vulnerabilities in running images (Amazon Inspector ECR/EKS findings, ECR scan findings for images actually used by running workloads — look for critical/high); AWS-7 node EBS volume encryption (launch templates block device mappings, default EBS encryption, actual attached volumes' Encrypted flag); AWS-8 node IMDSv2 (launch template MetadataOptions HttpTokens=required, hop limit, and actual EC2 instances' MetadataOptions).",
  "context": "User wants EVERY control assigned here to get a status (PASS / FAIL / MANUAL / NOT ASSESSABLE) with concrete evidence (API call used, key fields/values, resource IDs such as nodegroup names, launch template IDs/versions, instance IDs, volume IDs). Use only read-only AWS calls (eks list/describe nodegroups, fargate profiles, ec2 describe instances/volumes/launch-template-versions, ssm describe/get parameter, inspector2 list findings, ecr describe-image-scan-findings, etc.). Kubelet file permission and config checks normally require node shell access or kubelet config read; if you cannot reach nodes (e.g. SSM not available/permitted) say so and mark those controls NOT ASSESSABLE or infer only from AWS evidence that is genuinely conclusive (e.g. launch template user data / AMI type / kubelet config in user data) — do NOT guess or fabricate. Do not run commands on nodes or mutate anything. Use the AWS docs lookup tool to confirm exact v1.8.0 control IDs/titles if unsure; list every control individually.",
  "resources": ["EKS cluster cis-skill-test", "us-east-1", "account 012345678901_1"],
  "criteria": "CRITICAL: Keep an explicit log of EVERY read call that was denied or errored (AccessDenied, UnauthorizedOperation, etc.): exact service:Action, resource, and error text, and for each denial list which control IDs could not be fully verified because of it. Return a table: Control ID | Title | Status | Evidence, followed by a 'Denied reads' table: Call | Error | Controls affected. Another agent covers cluster-level controls (CIS sections 2, 4, 5, AWS-1, AWS-2, AWS-4, AWS-5, AWS-9) — do not duplicate them."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check node-level EKS CIS controls and AWS-3, 6, 7, 8"}], "created_at": null}

